# Nothing BitBake writes belongs in the repository. The build tree lives
# outside it anyway (see scripts/common.sh); these are the strays.
build/
tmp/
sstate-cache/
downloads/

# And the layers themselves. kas clones poky, meta-openembedded and
# meta-raspberrypi into KAS_WORK_DIR, which is ~/bench; run without that
# variable set it falls back to paths relative to the kas file and clones a
# second set in here, 469 MB of them, which nothing then uses.
#
# Ignored rather than merely warned about because of what they were
# actually costing: scripts/archive.sh stamps each stored image with the
# commit and appends -dirty when git status is not clean, so every archive
# taken on that host claimed to come from a modified tree. It did not. The
# record was wrong about the one thing it exists to get right.
#
# scripts/common.sh warns when they are present, since ignoring a stray is
# not the same as wanting one.
poky/
meta-openembedded/
meta-raspberrypi/
*.wic
*.wic.bz2
*.wic.bmap
*.manifest
*.rootfs.*

# SDK output and the cross-compiled example.
sdk/hello-gpiod/hello-gpiod
*.sh.sdk

# Editor and OS noise.
*~
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Evidence is committed on purpose, so nothing under projects/*/docs is here.

# Byte code from running the Python programs out of the tree during tests.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Credentials the boards read from their boot partition. The design keeps
# these off the card image and out of the repository on purpose: the image
# carries the capability, the card carries the identity. See
# meta-bench/recipes-bench/bench-router/files/bench-router-setup.
#
# Named here anyway, because the failure is silent and permanent. A boot
# partition copied off a card for safekeeping is a directory of ordinary
# files, and one of them holds an access point passphrase, a WAN passphrase
# and a SIM PIN. If that directory is ever moved into this tree, git would
# take it without comment and the history would be public.
router.conf
wifi.conf
